fixture_mean_here — The mean of a variable of the frame around the call, as a fixture  data · tier 1 · since 0.7.0 · 1.0 · exact

USAGE
    fixture_mean_here(var)

DESCRIPTION
    `mean` of `var` over the enclosing frame, or over its group under `by:`: the fixture of the enclosing
    frame beside an argument the call gives.

ARGUMENTS
    var         Var. The variable, of the frame the call stands in.

VALUE
    The mean, a Float.

WARNINGS AND NOTES
    Z0401   outside a frame method, where there is no frame around the call
    W0201   missing values skipped, with the count; all missing, or no rows at all, gives NA
    W0204   Inf and -Inf both present, so the result is NA
    Z0101   no such variable in the frame
    Z0102   a variable that differs only in case from the name written

ACCURACY
    Exact.

SEE ALSO
    mean, n

EXAMPLES
    > let d = frame(x = [1, 2, 6], g = ["a", "a", "b"])
    > d.aggregate(m = fixture_mean_here(x), by: g)
    frame · 2 rows × 2 variables

          g     m
      1   a   1.5
      2   b     6
